abstract: >
  Lean 4 formalization of the neutral structural substrate of Structural
  Explainability. The theory provides propositional languages, commitment
  theories and consequence, interpretive frameworks, referent carriers,
  and referential regimes composed from distinct abstract individuation,
  co-reference, and persistence accounts. It formalizes substrate commitments,
  attribution, framework-relative properties, interpretive non-commitment,
  extension stability, neutrality, and neutrality by design. Under referential
  common ground, foundational restriction is proved sufficient for neutrality.
  The full neutrality constraint is an explicit condition on realizations.

